{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1010039-the-wild-west-the-yndicate-and-prostitutes","id":1010039,"title":"The Wild West, the $yndicate, and Prostitutes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-29T19:58:23-08:00","id":1010039,"title":"The Wild West, the $yndicate, and Prostitutes","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c26b-ym5GGE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c26b-ym5GGE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c26b-ym5GGE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/c26b-ym5GGE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr </b>Prostitutes were the major power players in civilizing the Wild West. They made work camps into actual towns and used the money they made to help their communities and local businesses.<br /> <br /> The creators of &quot;Adam Ruins Everything&quot; are pretty good about citing their sources (wine episode aside), so I'm willing to bet that this is (at least partially) true. It made me think about some ladies of the night awakening and becoming members of the $yndicate. World's oldest profession, right? It'd be interesting to see some $ynidcate controlled Wild West towns run by prostitutes instead of railroad barons. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T21:40:20-08:00","id":1010051,"title":"","content":"They're not wrong, though they neglect the role of two other groups: Fraternal societies (which sprang up overnight anywhere with a modest population and a couple of buildings in the Wild West and played a major role in the same things that video lauds (the provision of services, education, disaster relief, worker's comp, protection from violence, etc) and perhaps more importantly, the people controlling the prostitutes. The West did see many strong women rise to control their own brothels, but it also saw plenty of savage, violent brutes like Al Swearengen do the same thing, and there were more of those than there were of self-organizing, self-ruling brothels.<br /> <br /> The notion of the Syndicate controlling prostitution is certainly an interesting one, and suggests a natural source of conflict with Setites and the Cult of Ecstasy over the business, and with the more zealous and Christian Choristers over the morality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:35:44-08:00","id":1013659,"title":"","content":"Considering their history as the High Guild and the fact that their magic is based on Ars Cupidae and manipulating people's desires and needs, I would be quite surprised that The Oldest Trade in the World has not always been under their thumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:44:10-08:00","id":1014787,"title":"","content":"This is significantly before even the High Guild, but some of the proto-HG groups were probably involved. One of the first things the Romans would do when they took over a region, even before ensuring Latin was commonly spoken, was standardize prostitution. To that end, they minted coins with sex acts on them and distributed them to the soldiers. They were a combination form of payment and means of communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T20:15:20-08:00","id":1015134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1010039-the-wild-west-the-yndicate-and-prostitutes?p=1014787#post1014787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is significantly before even the High Guild, but some of the proto-HG groups were probably involved. One of the first things the Romans would do when they took over a region, even before ensuring Latin was commonly spoken, was standardize prostitution. To that end, they minted coins with sex acts on them and distributed them to the soldiers. They were a combination form of payment and means of communication.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa, seriously? That's awesome, source?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:36:01-08:00","id":1016088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmegaZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1010039-the-wild-west-the-yndicate-and-prostitutes?p=1015134#post1015134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Whoa, seriously? That's awesome, source?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm now rather disappointed because when I went to look up the name of these things, it turns out there's a lot of disagreement among historians about what they were actually for. They do exist though. They are called Spintriae (singular: Sprintria). They are actually available on ebay if you want to see what they look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:00:38-08:00","id":1016209,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Ambiguously historical is good enough for me (and Mage lol)! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}